  "narrative": {
    "summary": "Empirical evaluation on 25,000 IMDB test reviews reveals clear trade-offs between architectural complexity and sequence memory.",
    "accuracy_comparison": "LSTM surpassed Simple RNN by 26.44% in test accuracy and 0.1865 in F1-score. This reflects LSTM's ability to maintain a continuous gradient highway via its cell state.",
    "training_speed_comparison": "Simple RNN required fewer floating point operations per recurrent step (1 matrix multiply vs 4 in LSTM), resulting in training speed that was approximately 2.9x faster.",
    "long_dependency_comparison": "In sequence evaluations, Simple RNN experiences vanishing gradients when sequences exceed 50-100 timesteps due to repeated tanh matrix multiplications. LSTM mitigates this through additive cell state updates and forget gates, preserving distant sentiment markers more robustly.",
    "limitations": "These findings are observed with a vocabulary of 10,000 tokens, 64 hidden units, and 5 epochs. Exact performance is subject to hyperparameter choices, random initialization seed, and hardware batching constraints."
  }
